{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1404792-so-it-s-not-just-me-lower-power-more-paradigm-oriented","id":1404792,"title":"So It's not Just Me - Lower Power, More \"Paradigm\" Oriented!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-07-26T09:57:44-07:00","id":1404792,"title":"So It's not Just Me - Lower Power, More \"Paradigm\" Oriented!","content":"In the past 2 days we've had 2 threads with a common theme, that they want to use the slick, slick mechanics of MtA 2e (which even many Mage the Ascension fans think have better mechanics) by. Like my own threads, many of the common ideas are<br /> <br /> 1. lowering the power level;<br /> 2. making it feel more &quot;real-world&quot; magical - a focus on the mage's paradigm (e.g., Hermetic magic, Witchcraft), more rituals vs fast casting, etc.<br /> <br /> M20 has a book that does just this for Mage the Awakening<br /> <br /> There's some sort of market for this, because (a) it was done for M20, (b) people keep asking for advice about it.<br /> <br /> It seems like this wouldn't be that hard to do for someone that understood the system better? Can one of you that understands the system well just do this and put it on storyteller's vault so I could just pay for it? I'm a bit confused by the system as is.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T11:24:22-07:00","id":1404810,"title":"","content":"I would say some design elements to consider could be:<br /> <br /> 1- Define the limitations, making them consistent rather than arbitrary.<br /> <br /> 2- Increase the focus on yantras, with more power requiring sacrifice of resources (consumables, rare materials, taking damage, etc)<br /> <br /> 3- Account for the different flow of problemsolving, since improvizing solutions will be less likely. Imbued items will have more value<br /> <br /> 4- Construct a standard system for creating, exploring and expanding on a paradigm. The Mystery Cult and Shadow Name merits already present a skeleton for this<br /> <br /> 5- Redefine how to lure mages into incurring Paradox. Normally its desperation or hubris that lead them down the path of quick and dirty solutions. But if everything requires a ritual and setup, a much greater focus will be placed in securing resources. This in turn makes the likelihood of Paradox decrease unless you artificially instill a sense of scarcity into the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-26-2020, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T11:37:02-07:00","id":1404812,"title":"","content":"Here's a thread that had some mechanical tinkering ideas<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic\"> Gritty, Dirty, Dangerous Magic - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1104715-gritty-dirty-dangerous-magic </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I love this quote from this thread (http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/774491-2nd-what-you-guys-liked-or-disliked-in-mtaw-2nd/page3) , and would love to run a Mage Chronicle at a bit lower power level, more gritty and dangerous. What would you need to tinker with to make your chronicle work this way? I feel that Hurt Locker would have lots of good stuff for making violence a bit more gritty. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T13:50:42-07:00","id":1404827,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure what there'd be to add about 'paradigm' beyond just doing it. Like, there are a bunch of open ended yantra which are going to be shaped by your mage's ideas, so just use them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}